# Match on an annotated unit constructor must succeed (S-855 bug fix, maintained in S-944).
# The Field and Call arms in match_pattern must peel Value::Annotated wrappers before matching.
# Red@[category: "primary"] evaluates to Value::Annotated { inner: Variant("MyType.Red", None), .. }.
# Before the fix, the Field arm fell through to _ => Ok(None), causing the wildcard to fire.
# After the fix, peel_annotated(value.clone()) is applied and the inner Variant tag "MyType.Red" is matched.
# Uses MyType.Red as scrutinee (T-1086: qualified form is in typecheck scope; unqualified Red is not).
[
  MyType:  [type Red@[category: "primary"]: []]
  matched: [match MyType.Red
    MyType.Red: "matched"
    ...:        "wildcard"]
  result:  [= matched "matched"]
]
=== out
Dict({"MyType": Dict({"Red": Variant(MyType.Red, Null)}), "matched": String("matched"), "result": Variant(Boolean.True, Null)})
